From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 20:53:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] CarrierConfigManager: require IMS provisioning for VOICE over
 IWLAN by default

A modem that will not accept a Wi-Fi calling configuration it has not been told is provisioned
answers the attempt and declines it:

    client_provisioning_config_ind_hdlr: .. client_prov_enabled: 0
                                         .. wifi_call_preference: 0    (1 was sent)

ImsManager.isWfcProvisionedOnDevice() only reaches the branch that pushes the provisioning value
when isMmTelProvisioningRequired(VOICE, IWLAN) is true. With KEY_MMTEL_REQUIRES_PROVISIONING_BUNDLE
defaulting to an empty bundle it short-circuits to "provisioned" locally, ENABLE_VOWIFI is never
sent, and the modem is left believing the feature is unprovisioned while the framework believes it
is enabled.

VOICE over IWLAN only. VoLTE falls through to the deprecated
KEY_CARRIER_VOLTE_PROVISIONING_REQUIRED_BOOL, which stays false, so it is untouched -- and it has
never needed this path, because it works off the modem's own carrier config. Wi-Fi calling, which
that config does not enable, is exactly the feature that does need it.

Set here rather than in a device carrier_config overlay because a nested <pbundle_as_map> does not
survive that path. PersistableBundle.restoreFromXml() is called with throwException=false so a
malformed config cannot be used to attack the platform, which means a nested bundle it cannot parse
is dropped in silence. The XML compiles into the APK correctly -- verified with aapt2, attributes
and all -- and simply never appears in the merged config, while every scalar around it applies. It
looks exactly like a change that worked.
---
 .../telephony/CarrierConfigManager.java       | 29 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/telephony/java/android/telephony/CarrierConfigManager.java b/telephony/java/android/telephony/CarrierConfigManager.java
index 741721d14ac1..bd9126ac7cdb 100644
--- a/telephony/java/android/telephony/CarrierConfigManager.java
+++ b/telephony/java/android/telephony/CarrierConfigManager.java
@@ -47,6 +47,7 @@ import android.telephony.ims.ImsRegistrationAttributes;
 import android.telephony.ims.ImsSsData;
 import android.telephony.ims.RcsUceAdapter;
 import android.telephony.ims.feature.MmTelFeature;
+import android.telephony.ims.stub.ImsRegistrationImplBase;
 import android.telephony.ims.feature.RcsFeature;
 
 import com.android.internal.telephony.ICarrierConfigLoader;
@@ -5641,8 +5642,34 @@ public class CarrierConfigManager {
             /**
              * @see #KEY_MMTEL_REQUIRES_PROVISIONING_BUNDLE
              */
+            // Require IMS provisioning for VOICE over IWLAN by default.
+            //
+            // This device's modem will not accept a Wi-Fi calling configuration it has not been told
+            // is provisioned. It answers the attempt and declines it:
+            //
+            //     client_provisioning_config_ind_hdlr: .. client_prov_enabled: 0
+            //                                          .. wifi_call_preference: 0   (1 was sent)
+            //
+            // ImsManager.isWfcProvisionedOnDevice() only reaches the branch that pushes the
+            // provisioning value when isMmTelProvisioningRequired(VOICE, IWLAN) is true. With this
+            // bundle empty it short-circuits to "provisioned" locally, so ENABLE_VOWIFI is never
+            // sent and the modem is left believing the feature is unprovisioned.
+            //
+            // VOICE over IWLAN only, so VoLTE is untouched: it falls through to the deprecated
+            // KEY_CARRIER_VOLTE_PROVISIONING_REQUIRED_BOOL, which stays false. VoLTE works because
+            // the modem's own carrier config enables it and so never needed this path -- Wi-Fi
+            // calling, which that config does not enable, is exactly the feature that does.
+            //
+            // Set here rather than in a device carrier_config overlay because a nested
+            // <pbundle_as_map> does not survive that path: PersistableBundle.restoreFromXml() is
+            // called with throwException=false so the platform cannot be attacked with a malformed
+            // config, which means a nested bundle it cannot parse is dropped in silence. The XML
+            // compiles into the APK correctly and simply never appears in the merged config.
+            PersistableBundle mmtelProvisioning = new PersistableBundle();
+            mmtelProvisioning.putIntArray(Ims.KEY_CAPABILITY_TYPE_VOICE_INT_ARRAY,
+                    new int[] { ImsRegistrationImplBase.REGISTRATION_TECH_IWLAN });
             defaults.putPersistableBundle(
-                    KEY_MMTEL_REQUIRES_PROVISIONING_BUNDLE, new PersistableBundle());
+                    KEY_MMTEL_REQUIRES_PROVISIONING_BUNDLE, mmtelProvisioning);
             /**
              * @see #KEY_RCS_REQUIRES_PROVISIONING_BUNDLE
              */
